# Source offer for the programs in this image

This image contains the Cipherframe server (Apache-2.0) and, as separate programs that the server
starts as processes, the third-party software below. FFmpeg and x264 are licensed under the GNU
General Public License, so the FFmpeg binaries in this image are GPL-licensed (see
`COPYING.GPLv2` and `COPYING.GPLv3` in this directory). They are not linked into the Cipherframe
server. This file is generated by `build/worker.Dockerfile` from the pins used for the build.

## Corresponding source

| Program | Version | Source | SHA-256 |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| FFmpeg | @FFMPEG_VERSION@ | https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-@FFMPEG_VERSION@.tar.xz | @FFMPEG_SHA256@ |
| x264 (GPL-2.0-or-later) | `stable` branch, commit @X264_COMMIT@ | https://code.videolan.org/videolan/x264/-/archive/@X264_COMMIT@/x264-@X264_COMMIT@.tar.bz2 | @X264_SHA256@ |
| dav1d (BSD-2-Clause) | @DAV1D_VERSION@ | https://downloads.videolan.org/pub/videolan/dav1d/@DAV1D_VERSION@/dav1d-@DAV1D_VERSION@.tar.xz | @DAV1D_SHA256@ |
| GNU C Library (LGPL-2.1-or-later), linked statically | Debian @LIBC_VERSION@ | `apt-get source libc6` using http://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian/@DEBIAN_SNAPSHOT@/ (bookworm main) | not applicable |

## How it was built

The build script is `build/worker.Dockerfile` in the Cipherframe repository
(https://github.com/venkataPhanindraVutla/cipherframe). It builds x264 and dav1d as static
libraries and then FFmpeg, whose configuration is (the same text is printed by
`ffmpeg -hide_banner -buildconf`):

```
@BUILDCONF@
```

Because the programs are linked statically, the glibc object files are inside the binaries. With
the build script and the sources above you can rebuild and relink them.

## Written offer

If you received this image and want the complete corresponding source of FFmpeg or x264 as
distributed here, the URLs above are the exact sources. Should they become unavailable, contact the
Cipherframe maintainers through the channel in the repository's `SECURITY.md` and a copy will be
provided for at least three years after you received the image.
